{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useHotkeyRecorder(options): ReactHotkeyRecorder;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHotkeyRecorder.ts#L58","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHotkeyRecorder.ts:58"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React hook for recording keyboard shortcuts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook provides a thin wrapper around the framework-agnostic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":"\nclass, managing all the complexity of capturing keyboard events, converting them\nto hotkey strings, and handling edge cases like Escape to cancel or Backspace/Delete\nto clear."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyRecorderOptions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration options for the recorder"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/ReactHotkeyRecorder.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReactHotkeyRecorder"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An object with recording state and control functions"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function ShortcutSettings() {\n  const [shortcut, setShortcut] = useState<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\n  const recorder = useHotkeyRecorder({\n    onRecord: (hotkey) => {\n      setShortcut(hotkey)\n    },\n    onCancel: () => {\n      console.log('Recording cancelled')\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={recorder.startRecording}>\n        {recorder.isRecording ? 'Recording...' : 'Edit Shortcut'}\n      </button>\n      {recorder.recordedHotkey && (\n        <div>Recording: {recorder.recordedHotkey}</div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeyRecorder(options): ReactHotkeyRecorder;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeyRecorder.ts:58](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHotkeyRecorder.ts#L58)\n\nReact hook for recording keyboard shortcuts.\n\nThis hook provides a thin wrapper around the framework-agnostic `HotkeyRecorder`\nclass, managing all the complexity of capturing keyboard events, converting them\nto hotkey strings, and handling edge cases like Escape to cancel or Backspace/Delete\nto clear.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n`HotkeyRecorderOptions`\n\nConfiguration options for the recorder\n\n## Returns\n\n[`ReactHotkeyRecorder`](../interfaces/ReactHotkeyRecorder.md)\n\nAn object with recording state and control functions\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction ShortcutSettings() {\n  const [shortcut, setShortcut] = useState<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\n  const recorder = useHotkeyRecorder({\n    onRecord: (hotkey) => {\n      setShortcut(hotkey)\n    },\n    onCancel: () => {\n      console.log('Recording cancelled')\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={recorder.startRecording}>\n        {recorder.isRecording ? 'Recording...' : 'Edit Shortcut'}\n      </button>\n      {recorder.recordedHotkey && (\n        <div>Recording: {recorder.recordedHotkey}</div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useHotkeyRecorder\ntitle: useHotkeyRecorder\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeyRecorder(options): ReactHotkeyRecorder;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeyRecorder.ts:58](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHotkeyRecorder.ts#L58)\n\nReact hook for recording keyboard shortcuts.\n\nThis hook provides a thin wrapper around the framework-agnostic `HotkeyRecorder`\nclass, managing all the complexity of capturing keyboard events, converting them\nto hotkey strings, and handling edge cases like Escape to cancel or Backspace/Delete\nto clear.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n`HotkeyRecorderOptions`\n\nConfiguration options for the recorder\n\n## Returns\n\n[`ReactHotkeyRecorder`](../interfaces/ReactHotkeyRecorder.md)\n\nAn object with recording state and control functions\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction ShortcutSettings() {\n  const [shortcut, setShortcut] = useState<Hotkey>('Mod+S')\n\n  const recorder = useHotkeyRecorder({\n    onRecord: (hotkey) => {\n      setShortcut(hotkey)\n    },\n    onCancel: () => {\n      console.log('Recording cancelled')\n    },\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <button onClick={recorder.startRecording}>\n        {recorder.isRecording ? 'Recording...' : 'Edit Shortcut'}\n      </button>\n      {recorder.recordedHotkey && (\n        <div>Recording: {recorder.recordedHotkey}</div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
